SpinWeightedSpheroidalHarmonicS"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3c1b8041-22a3-4fbb-8add-4f13fd2c6fa8"],
 " aims to produce a numerical value with the maximum possible precision \
given the precision of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "\[Gamma]"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0e3455b7-5a1a-47e0-8775-4e903c39a14d"],
 "."
}], "Notes",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.893617185702352*^9, {3.893784049188861*^9, 3.893784056146166*^9}, {
   3.893784105178963*^9, 3.893784138520361*^9}},
 CellID->398291475,ExpressionUUID->"17d6d630-3880-4438-9805-ab63a93552c7"],

Cell["\<\
Numerical values are computed using either Leaver's method or an expansion in \
terms of spin-weighted spherical harmonics.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.893617192128092*^9},
 CellID->378292626,ExpressionUUID->"46c5913e-84bc-43bf-a1b5-7e08d9b90f51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The number of terms used for numerical evaluation is such that the \
normalisation is determined as accurately as possible given the precision of \
the input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "\[Gamma]"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "66e8c724-7906-4d7d-ae98-1c22918b1406"],
 "."
}], "Notes",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.893617199430872*^9, {3.89378408783881*^9, 3.893784088838727*^9}},
 CellID->1412570062,ExpressionUUID->"60b7c213-6208-467b-9d87-826ef9a1f1ed"],

